Rem ==================================================================
Rem seedephemeris.shoddy — reckoner seed: ephemeris.shoddy, at a
Rem keyboard
Rem
Rem The sky from a prompt: sidereal time, the sun and the moon as sky
Rem positions, the moon's phase, age, distance, rise and set, the five
Rem naked-eye planets, the observer transform and the separation
Rem between two sky positions.
Rem
Rem THE SHAPES ARE SEEDGEO'S, ONE SPHERE LATER. A point on the Earth is
Rem the two-element LIST seedgeo established, { 53.72 -1.86 }, latitude
Rem first. A SKY position is the same shape one frame up:
Rem { ra dec }, right ascension then declination, both degrees — built
Rem by EPHSUN, EPHMOON and EPHPLANET, consumed by EPHALTAZ and
Rem EPHSEPARATION. What an observer sees is { alt az }. Nothing here
Rem needs a new spelling, only the discipline to keep the two kinds of
Rem list apart, which the guards below enforce by refusing a
Rem declination outside -90..90.
Rem
Rem A DATE IS A JULIAN DAY NUMBER, made by JULDAYNUMBER (seedjulian) or
Rem GEOJULIAN (seedgeo) — this seed mints no dates of its own, because
Rem the calendar is julian's and the bridge already exists. Hours are
Rem UTC, fractional, exactly as the sun words take them.
Rem
Rem NOTHING HERE ABORTS. ephemeris.shoddy's one abort is EphPlanet's
Rem chooser; the same test is asked here first and refused with the
Rem same words. Every malformed list, string or fraction is a refusal
Rem that leaves the stack exactly as it was.
Rem
Rem AN Option BRIDGES AS A ONE-CELL LIST — { } for None, { h } for a
Rem rise at h — the encoding seedgeo's sun words and seedbool's LOWBIT
Rem already use, and for the same reason: a word must push exactly one
Rem cell or UNDO's accounting breaks. A circumpolar moon's rise is
Rem { }, which is the honest stack spelling of "it does not".
Rem ==================================================================

Include "ephemeris.shoddy"
Include "geo.shoddy"
Include "cuttle.shoddy"
Include "reckoner.shoddy"
Include "seq.shoddy"

Rem ---- reading the arguments off the stack -------------------------------

Rem A Cell holding { lat lon } as a GeoPt — seedgeo's reader, respelled
Rem with this seed's prefix because two seeds may not share a Def.
Def EsPt(word As String, c As Cell) As Result
    Select Case RckListArg(word, c)
        Case Ok(xs)
            EsPtOf(word, xs)
        Case Err(w, at)
            Err(w, at)
        Case Else
            Err(word & " did not answer", 0)

Def EsPtOf(word As String, xs As List Of Cell) As Result
    If Length(xs) <> 2 Then
        Err(word & " needs a point as a LIST of a latitude and a longitude, got " & Str(Length(xs)) & " items", 0)
    Else
        EsPtNums(word, xs)

Def EsPtNums(word As String, xs As List Of Cell) As Result
    Select Case Pair(RckNumArg(word, Nth(xs, 1)), RckNumArg(word, Nth(xs, 2)))
        Case Pair(Ok(lat), Ok(lon))
            EsChecked(word, GeoTryAt(lat, lon))
        Case Else
            Err(word & " needs a point as a LIST of two NUMBERs", 0)

Def EsChecked(word As String, r As Result) As Result
    Select Case r
        Case Ok(p)
            Ok(p)
        Case Err(w, at)
            Err(word & ": " & w, at)
        Case Else
            Err(word & " did not answer", 0)

Rem A Cell holding { ra dec } as an EphSky. The declination is range
Rem checked — a sky list and a point list are the same shape, and a
Rem latitude-first point handed to a sky word would otherwise compute
Rem a plausible nonsense; a dec beyond the poles is the tell.
Def EsSky(word As String, c As Cell) As Result
    Select Case RckListArg(word, c)
        Case Ok(xs)
            EsSkyOf(word, xs)
        Case Err(w, at)
            Err(w, at)
        Case Else
            Err(word & " did not answer", 0)

Def EsSkyOf(word As String, xs As List Of Cell) As Result
    If Length(xs) <> 2 Then
        Err(word & " needs a sky position as a LIST of a right ascension and a declination, got " & Str(Length(xs)) & " items", 0)
    Else
        EsSkyNums(word, xs)

Def EsSkyNums(word As String, xs As List Of Cell) As Result
    Select Case Pair(RckNumArg(word, Nth(xs, 1)), RckNumArg(word, Nth(xs, 2)))
        Case Pair(Ok(ra), Ok(dec))
            EsSkyMade(word, ra, dec)
        Case Else
            Err(word & " needs a sky position as a LIST of two NUMBERs", 0)

Def EsSkyMade(word As String, ra As Number, dec As Number) As Result
    If Not (dec >= -90 And dec <= 90) Then
        Err(word & ": A DECLINATION OF " & Str(dec) & " IS OUTSIDE -90..90 — IS THIS A POINT WHERE A SKY POSITION SHOULD BE?", 0)
    Else
        Ok(EphSky(ra, dec))

Rem ---- writing the answers back ------------------------------------------

Def EsSkyCell(sky As EphSky) As Cell
    CutList({ CutNum(EphRa(sky)), CutNum(EphDec(sky)) })

Def EsViewCell(v As EphView) As Cell
    CutList({ CutNum(EphAlt(v)), CutNum(EphAzim(v)) })

Rem { } for None, { h } for Some — the one-cell Option encoding every
Rem seed uses.
Def EsOptCell(o As Option) As Cell
    Select Case o
        Case Some(x)
            CutList({ CutNum(x) })
        Case Else
            CutList({ })

Rem ---- the shapes the words share -----------------------------------------

Rem Most words here end with a Julian date and an hour: read both as
Rem numbers, then hand on.
Def EsJdHours(word As String, a As Cell, b As Cell, f As [ Number Number -- Cell ]) As RckWork
    Select Case Pair(RckNumArg(word, a), RckNumArg(word, b))
        Case Pair(Ok(jd), Ok(hours))
            RckVals({ Call(f, jd, hours) })
        Case Else
            RckWorkBad(word & " needs a Julian date and an hour, both NUMBERs")

Rem ---- sidereal time -------------------------------------------------------

Def EsSeedSidereal(st As RckState) As RckState
    RckReg(st, "EPHSIDEREAL", 2, RckPure(Fn(vs) => EsSidereal(vs)), "( jd h -- deg )", "Greenwich mean sidereal time at that UTC hour, degrees 0..360. Add an east longitude for the local form.")

Def EsSidereal(vs As List Of Cell) As RckWork
    EsJdHours("EPHSIDEREAL", Nth(vs, 1), Nth(vs, 2), Fn(jd, hours) => CutNum(EphSidereal(jd, hours)))

Rem ---- the bodies -----------------------------------------------------------

Def EsSeedSun(st As RckState) As RckState
    RckReg(st, "EPHSUN", 2, RckPure(Fn(vs) => EsSun(vs)), "( jd h -- sky )", "The sun as a sky position, { ra dec } in degrees. For rise and set at a place, GEOSUNRISE is the word; this one is for the sky.")

Def EsSun(vs As List Of Cell) As RckWork
    EsJdHours("EPHSUN", Nth(vs, 1), Nth(vs, 2), Fn(jd, hours) => EsSkyCell(EphSun(jd, hours)))

Def EsSeedMoon(st As RckState) As RckState
    Let s1 = RckReg(st, "EPHMOON", 2, RckPure(Fn(vs) => EsMoon(vs)), "( jd h -- sky )", "The moon as a sky position, { ra dec } in degrees, geocentric, to about a third of a degree.")
    Let s2 = RckReg(s1, "EPHMOONDIST", 2, RckPure(Fn(vs) => EsMoondist(vs)), "( jd h -- m )", "The distance to the moon in metres, from its parallax.")
    Let s3 = RckReg(s2, "EPHMOONPHASE", 2, RckPure(Fn(vs) => EsMoonphase(vs)), "( jd h -- f )", "The illuminated fraction, 0 at new through 1 at full.")
    RckReg(s3, "EPHMOONAGE", 2, RckPure(Fn(vs) => EsMoonage(vs)), "( jd h -- days )", "Days since new moon, 0 up to a synodic month of 29.53 — what says waxing or waning when the fraction alone cannot.")

Def EsMoon(vs As List Of Cell) As RckWork
    EsJdHours("EPHMOON", Nth(vs, 1), Nth(vs, 2), Fn(jd, hours) => EsSkyCell(EphMoon(jd, hours)))

Def EsMoondist(vs As List Of Cell) As RckWork
    EsJdHours("EPHMOONDIST", Nth(vs, 1), Nth(vs, 2), Fn(jd, hours) => CutNum(EphMoonDistance(jd, hours)))

Def EsMoonphase(vs As List Of Cell) As RckWork
    EsJdHours("EPHMOONPHASE", Nth(vs, 1), Nth(vs, 2), Fn(jd, hours) => CutNum(EphMoonPhase(jd, hours)))

Def EsMoonage(vs As List Of Cell) As RckWork
    EsJdHours("EPHMOONAGE", Nth(vs, 1), Nth(vs, 2), Fn(jd, hours) => CutNum(EphMoonAge(jd, hours)))

Rem ---- moonrise and moonset -------------------------------------------------

Def EsSeedMoonRise(st As RckState) As RckState
    Let s1 = RckReg(st, "EPHMOONRISE", 2, RckPure(Fn(vs) => EsMoonrise(vs)), "( p jd -- hs )", "UTC hours of moonrise on that day as { h }, or { } - roughly once a month a day genuinely has none, and near a pole the moon can be up or down for weeks.")
    RckReg(s1, "EPHMOONSET", 2, RckPure(Fn(vs) => EsMoonset(vs)), "( p jd -- hs )", "UTC hours of moonset, { h } or { }, on the same terms as EPHMOONRISE.")

Def EsMoonrise(vs As List Of Cell) As RckWork
    EsMoonEvent("EPHMOONRISE", vs, EphMoonRise)

Def EsMoonset(vs As List Of Cell) As RckWork
    EsMoonEvent("EPHMOONSET", vs, EphMoonSet)

Def EsMoonEvent(word As String, vs As List Of Cell, f As [ GeoPt Number -- Option ]) As RckWork
    Select Case EsPt(word, Nth(vs, 1))
        Case Ok(p)
            EsMoonEventAt(word, p, Nth(vs, 2), f)
        Case Err(w, at)
            RckWorkBad(w)
        Case Else
            RckWorkBad(word & " did not answer")

Def EsMoonEventAt(word As String, p As GeoPt, c As Cell, f As [ GeoPt Number -- Option ]) As RckWork
    Select Case RckNumArg(word, c)
        Case Ok(jd)
            RckVals({ EsOptCell(Call(f, p, jd)) })
        Case Err(w, at)
            RckWorkBad(w)
        Case Else
            RckWorkBad(word & " did not answer")

Rem ---- the planets ------------------------------------------------------------

Def EsSeedPlanets(st As RckState) As RckState
    Let s1 = RckReg(st, "EPHMERCURY", 0, RckPure(Fn(vs) => RckVals({ CutNum(EphMercury()) })), "( -- planet )", "Mercury, for EPHPLANET.")
    Let s2 = RckReg(s1, "EPHVENUS", 0, RckPure(Fn(vs) => RckVals({ CutNum(EphVenus()) })), "( -- planet )", "Venus, for EPHPLANET.")
    Let s3 = RckReg(s2, "EPHMARS", 0, RckPure(Fn(vs) => RckVals({ CutNum(EphMars()) })), "( -- planet )", "Mars, for EPHPLANET. The numbering keeps the Earth's seat: Mars is 4.")
    Let s4 = RckReg(s3, "EPHJUPITER", 0, RckPure(Fn(vs) => RckVals({ CutNum(EphJupiter()) })), "( -- planet )", "Jupiter, for EPHPLANET.")
    Let s5 = RckReg(s4, "EPHSATURN", 0, RckPure(Fn(vs) => RckVals({ CutNum(EphSaturn()) })), "( -- planet )", "Saturn, for EPHPLANET.")
    RckReg(s5, "EPHPLANET", 3, RckPure(Fn(vs) => EsPlanet(vs)), "( planet jd h -- sky )", "A planet as a sky position, { ra dec } geocentric. Name it with EPHMERCURY through EPHSATURN.")

Rem The library's chooser guard, asked here first so the session
Rem refuses where the machine would abort — the same words, minus the
Rem death.
Def EsPlanet(vs As List Of Cell) As RckWork
    Select Case RckNumArg("EPHPLANET", Nth(vs, 1))
        Case Ok(which)
            EsPlanetAt(which, Nth(vs, 2), Nth(vs, 3))
        Case Err(w, at)
            RckWorkBad(w)
        Case Else
            RckWorkBad("EPHPLANET did not answer")

Def EsPlanetAt(which As Number, b As Cell, c As Cell) As RckWork
    If which = 3 Then
        RckWorkBad("EPHPLANET: PLANET 3 IS THE EARTH, WHICH IS WHERE YOU ARE STANDING — THE GEO WORDS ANSWER FOR IT")
    Else
        If which = 1 Or which = 2 Or which = 4 Or which = 5 Or which = 6 Then
            EsJdHours("EPHPLANET", b, c, Fn(jd, hours) => EsSkyCell(EphPlanet(which, jd, hours)))
        Else
            RckWorkBad("EPHPLANET: THERE IS NO PLANET '" & Str(which) & "' IN THE TABLE — USE EPHMERCURY THROUGH EPHSATURN")

Rem ---- the observer ------------------------------------------------------------

Def EsSeedAltAz(st As RckState) As RckState
    Let s1 = RckReg(st, "EPHALTAZ", 4, RckPure(Fn(vs) => EsAltaz(vs)), "( p sky jd h -- view )", "What an observer at p sees of a sky position at that instant: { altitude azimuth }, azimuth a compass bearing.")
    RckReg(s1, "EPHSEPARATION", 2, RckPure(Fn(vs) => EsSeparation(vs)), "( a b -- deg )", "The angle between two sky positions, degrees.")

Def EsAltaz(vs As List Of Cell) As RckWork
    Select Case Pair(EsPt("EPHALTAZ", Nth(vs, 1)), EsSky("EPHALTAZ", Nth(vs, 2)))
        Case Pair(Ok(p), Ok(sky))
            EsJdHours("EPHALTAZ", Nth(vs, 3), Nth(vs, 4), Fn(jd, hours) => EsViewCell(EphAltAz(p, sky, jd, hours)))
        Case Pair(Err(w, at), other)
            RckWorkBad(w)
        Case Pair(other, Err(w, at))
            RckWorkBad(w)
        Case Else
            RckWorkBad("EPHALTAZ did not answer")

Def EsSeparation(vs As List Of Cell) As RckWork
    Select Case Pair(EsSky("EPHSEPARATION", Nth(vs, 1)), EsSky("EPHSEPARATION", Nth(vs, 2)))
        Case Pair(Ok(a), Ok(b))
            RckVals({ CutNum(EphSeparation(a, b)) })
        Case Pair(Err(w, at), other)
            RckWorkBad(w)
        Case Pair(other, Err(w, at))
            RckWorkBad(w)
        Case Else
            RckWorkBad("EPHSEPARATION did not answer")

Rem ---- the seed ------------------------------------------------------------------

Def RckSeedEphemeris(st As RckState) As RckState
    Let s1 = EsSeedSidereal(RckSeeding(st, "seed-ephemeris"))
    Let s2 = EsSeedSun(s1)
    Let s3 = EsSeedMoon(s2)
    Let s4 = EsSeedMoonRise(s3)
    Let s5 = EsSeedPlanets(s4)
    EsSeedAltAz(s5)
